{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Bottled_Lightning","to":"Bottled Lightning"},{"from":"Ring_of_the_Snake","to":"Ring of the Snake"},{"from":"Incense_Burner","to":"Incense Burner"},{"from":"Spirit_Poop","to":"Spirit Poop"},{"from":"Gold-Plated_Cables","to":"Gold-Plated Cables"},{"from":"Golden_Eye","to":"Golden Eye"},{"from":"Bottled_Flame","to":"Bottled Flame"},{"from":"Cursed_Key","to":"Cursed Key"},{"from":"Ring_of_the_Serpent","to":"Ring of the Serpent"},{"from":"Dead_Branch","to":"Dead Branch"},{"from":"Chemical_X","to":"Chemical X"},{"from":"Face_of_Cleric","to":"Face of Cleric"},{"from":"Magic_Flower","to":"Magic Flower"},{"from":"Self-Forming_Clay","to":"Self-Forming Clay"},{"from":"Regal_Pillow","to":"Regal Pillow"},{"from":"Tungsten_Rod","to":"Tungsten Rod"},{"from":"Emotion_Chip","to":"Emotion Chip"}],"pages":{"2550":{"pageid":2550,"ns":0,"title":"Bottled Flame","revisions":[{"revid":56909,"parentid":50837,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Bottled Flame\n|Image       = BottledFlame.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Upon pickup, choose an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} card. <br>At the start of each combat, this card will be in your hand.\n|Flavor      = Inside the bottle resides a flame that eternally burns.\n}}\n{{R|Bottled Flame}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Bottled Flame}}.\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} event by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Bottled Flame}}).\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Wheel of Change}} event by earning {{R|Bottled Flame}} as a prize.\n* Can be obtained from {{E|The Colosseum}} event by choosing the {{Frame|VICTORY}} option and getting {{R|Bottled Flame}} as the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic reward.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Cannot be obtained from {{R|Calling Bell}} and \"Obtain Relic\" events that drop the relic without it being a combat reward. This means, for example, {{R|Bottled Flame}} can be obtained from {{E|Dead Adventurer}} if the [[Elite]] is beaten, but cannot be obtained if it is found from the {{Frame|Search}} option.\n* Can only be obtained if your deck has a non-{{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic&type:Attack|Starter Attack}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\nBottling a card is '''not''' the same as \"making it {{KW|Innate}}\", as there are a few quirks that only affect bottled cards:\n* A bottled card can't be removed from the player's deck.\n* A bottled card can still be [[Transform|transformed]] as normal. However, this will also un-bottle it and it will no longer be drawn in the opening hand. This effectively disables {{R|Bottled Flame}}.\n* A bottled card can be duplicated from effects such as {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} and {{E|Duplicator}}, but the duplicate will not be bottled.\n* A bottled card will still have its cost randomized by {{R|Snecko Eye}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Bottling {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} that apply debuffs can be useful to set up in fights (such as {{C|Uppercut}}, {{C|Sucker Punch}}, and {{C|Beam Cell}})\n* Bottling {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} that draw cards can be useful to draw into more options on turn 1 (such as {{C|Pommel Strike}} or {{C|Wheel Kick}})\n* Bottling powerful {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|attacks}} can be useful to instantly remove lower-HP enemies from the fight (such as {{C|Immolate}} or {{C|Sunder}})\n\n== Bugs ==\n* If a card is [[Transform|transformed]] (which will un-bottle it), {{R|Bottled Flame}}'s description will still read that the original card will start in the player's hand (even though it won't as the card doesn't exist anymore).\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Bottled Flame}} is one of relics in the \"bottle relic set\" which all allow the player to choose a card of a different type to start in their opening hand; the others being {{R|Bottled Lightning}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} and {{R|Bottled Tornado}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Bottled Flame no longer appears if all of your Attacks are starter cards.\n** Bottled Cards upgraded from Mind Bloom event have their description updated correctly.\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Wheel of Change event no longer makes you stuck if the only removable cards in your deck are bottled.\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Purchasing Bottle relics after removing the last possible card to bottle out of your deck will no longer softlock.\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Peace Pipe relic cannot get rid of Bottled cards anymore.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Fix for Bottled cards showing up in Wheel of Change event's Purge result.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Fixed crash when travelling to a new room while a Bottle relic's screen was open.\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Bottled Flame, Lightning, and Tornado will no longer spawn if there are no valid cards.\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Polished art for Bottled Flame, Lightning, and Tornado relics.\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Fixed issue where bottled cards + Duplication event caused issues.\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Bottled Lightning and Bottled Flame icons no longer appear during combat.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Bottle Flame and Bottled Lightning can no longer be given from Neow at the start of a run.\n** Bottled Flame is now Uncommon (was Rare)\n** When Bottled Flame and Lightning are unequipped (not sure how), the game no longer crashes.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2551":{"pageid":2551,"ns":0,"title":"Bottled Lightning","revisions":[{"revid":56910,"parentid":50838,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Bottled Lightning\n|Image       = BottledLightning.png\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Description = Upon pickup, choose a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card. <br>At the start of each combat, this card will be in your hand.\n|Flavor      = Peering into the swirling maelstrom, you see a part of yourself staring back.\n}}\n{{R|Bottled Lightning}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Bottled Lightning}}.\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Dead Adventurer}} event by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Bottled Lightning}}).\n* Can be obtained from the {{E|Wheel of Change}} event by earning {{R|Bottled Lightning}} as a prize.\n* Can be obtained from {{E|The Colosseum}} event by choosing the {{Frame|VICTORY!}} option and getting {{R|Bottled Lightning}} as the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic reward.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Cannot be obtained from {{R|Calling Bell}} and \"Obtain Relic\" events, that drop the relic without it being a combat reward. This means, for example, {{R|Bottled Lightning}} can be obtained from {{E|Dead Adventurer}} if the [[Elite]] is beaten, but cannot be obtained if it is found from the {{Frame|Search}} option.\n* Can only be obtained if your deck has a non-{{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic&type:Skill|Starter Skill}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\nBottling a card is '''not''' the same as \"making it {{KW|Innate}}\", as there are a few quirks that only affect bottled cards:\n* A bottled card can't be removed from the player's deck.\n* A bottled card can still be [[Transform|transformed]] as normal. However, this will also un-bottle it and it will no longer be drawn in the opening hand. This effectively disables {{R|Bottled Lightning}}.\n* A bottled card can be duplicated from effects such as {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} and {{E|Duplicator}}, but the duplicate will not be bottled.\n* A bottled card will still have its cost randomized by {{R|Snecko Eye}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Bottling {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|skills}} that apply debuffs can be useful to set up in fights (such as {{C|Disarm}} and {{C|Crippling Cloud}})\n* Bottling {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|skills}} that draw cards can be useful to draw into more options on turn 1 (such as {{C|Offering}}, {{C|Adrenaline}}, {{C|Seek}}, or {{C|Scrawl}})\n\n== Bugs ==\n* If a card is [[Transform|transformed]] (which will un-bottle it), {{R|Bottled Lightning}}'s description will still read that the original card will start in the player's hand (even though it won't as the card doesn't exist anymore).\n\n== Trivia ==\n* \"Lightning in a bottle\" is an idiom that means ''to attempt something that is difficult, challenging, rare, or overall unlikely to achieve''.\n** Often used as the verb phrase \"Try to catch lightning in a bottle\" or \"Try to capture lightning in a bottle\".\n** It's use is attributed to \n* {{R|Bottled Lightning}} is one of relics in the \"bottle relic set\" which all allow the player to choose a card of a different type to start in their opening hand; the others being {{R|Bottled Flame}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} and {{R|Bottled Tornado}} for {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Bottled Lightning no longer appears if all of your Skills are starter cards.\n** Bottled Cards upgraded from Mind Bloom event have their description updated correctly.\n* '''Weekly Patch 49: The Designer'''\n** Wheel of Change event no longer makes you stuck if the only removable cards in your deck are bottled.\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Purchasing Bottle relics after removing the last possible card to bottle out of your deck will no longer softlock.\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Peace Pipe relic cannot get rid of Bottled cards anymore.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** Fix for Bottled cards showing up in Wheel of Change event's Purge result.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Fixed crash when travelling to a new room while a Bottle relic's screen was open.\n* '''Weekly Patch 13: Thinking Ahead'''\n** Bottled Flame, Lightning, and Tornado will no longer spawn if there are no valid cards.\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Polished art for Bottled Flame, Lightning, and Tornado relics.\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Fixed issue where bottled cards + Duplication event caused issues.\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Potential Fix for an edge case Bottled Tornado/Lightning issue.\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Bottled Lightning and Bottled Flame icons no longer appear during combat.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Bottle Flame and Bottled Lightning can no longer be given from Neow at the start of a run.\n** Bottled Lightning is now Uncommon (was Rare)\n** When Bottled Flame and Lightning are unequipped (not sure how), the game no longer crashes.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2493":{"pageid":2493,"ns":0,"title":"Chemical X","revisions":[{"revid":56035,"parentid":55690,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Chemical X\n|Image       = ChemicalX.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = The effects of your cost X cards are increased by 2.\n|Flavor      = WARNING: Do not combine with sugar, spice, and everything nice.\n}}\n{{R|Chemical X}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Chemical X}} affects X-Cost cards even if they are played directly from the player's draw pile and no {{KW|Energy}} is spent on them, such as from effects like {{C|Havoc}}, {{C|Mayhem}}, and {{P|Distilled Chaos}}.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} affects X-Cost cards even when they are played as a duplicate or copy, such as from effects like {{C|Burst}}, {{C|Echo Form}}, and {{P|Duplication Potion}}.\n* While {{R|Chemical X}} is naturally useful with all X-Cost cards regardless of how much {{KW|Energy}} is spent on them, it notably allows all X-Cost cards to be played with 0 {{KW|Energy}} and still receive a significant benefit:\n** {{C|Whirlwind}} will deal 5 damage to all enemies 2 times.\n** {{C|Skewer}} will deal 7 damage to an enemy 2 times.\n** {{C|Doppelganger}} will grant +2 {{BD|Draw Card|cards drawn}} and +2 {{Icon|GE}}[[Energy]] next turn.\n** {{C|Malaise}} will lower an enemy's {{BD|Strength}} by 2, and apply 2 {{BD|Weak}} to them.\n** {{C|Reinforced Body}} will grant 7 {{KW|Block}} 2 times.\n** {{C|Tempest}} will {{KW|Channel}} 2 {{KW|Lightning|Lightning Orbs}}.\n** {{C|Multi-Cast}} will {{KW|Evoke}} the player's next {{KW|Orb}} 2 times.\n** {{C|Collect}} will put a {{C|Miracle}}+ into the player's hand on their next 2 turns.\n** {{C|Conjure Blade}} will shuffle an {{C|Expunger}} into the player's draw pile which deals 9 damage 2 times.\n** {{C|Transmutation}} will add 2 random {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless cards}} to the player's hand, which will cost 0 {{KW|Energy}} on that turn.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n<!-- Not super happy with how I worded this, but I also can't figure out if there's a better way to explain this interaction. You are highly encouraged to throw this out and re-write it if you think you can word it better! -->\n* {{R|Chemical X}} specifically increases the ''effect'' of X-Cost cards by 2; it does not make X-Cost cards \"behave as if 2 more {{KW|Energy}} was spent on them\" when considering effects that trigger based on a card's cost. For example, playing an X-Cost attack with 0 {{KW|Energy}} will '''NOT''' have it played twice from {{R|Necronomicon}}. If the X-Cost attack is played with 2 or more {{KW|Energy}}, then {{R|Necronomicon}} will play it twice and both copies will benefit from the X+2 effect of {{R|Chemical X}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Chemical X}}'s name is a play-on-words on how it affects X-Cost cards in some way.\n* {{R|Chemical X}} is a reference to the 1998 cartoon [https://powerpuffgirls.fandom.com/wiki/The_Powerpuff_Girls_(1998) The Powerpuff Girls], where the titular girls were created in a lab using a substance called \"Chemical X\".\n** The flavor text is a direct reference to the series, featuring the iconic opening narration; ''Sugar, spice, and everything nice. These were the ingredients chosen to create the perfect little girl. But Professor Utonium added an extra ingredient to the concoction... '''Chemical X'''! Thus, The Powerpuff Girls were born!''.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 35: Aggregate'''\n** Adding shop relic Chemical X.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2490":{"pageid":2490,"ns":0,"title":"Cursed Key","revisions":[{"revid":56954,"parentid":55718,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Cursed Key\n|Image       = CursedKey.png\n|Rarity      = Boss\n|Description = Gain 1 {{KW|Energy}} at the start of your turn. Whenever you open a non-Boss chest, obtain a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n|Flavor      = You can feel the malicious energy emanating from the key. Power comes at a price.\n|GivesToPlayer = Energy\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}\n{{R|Cursed Key}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]]. It grants 1 {{KW|Energy}} at the start of each turn in combat, at the cost of adding a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} to the player's deck any time they open a non-Boss [[Chest]]. The {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} that gets added to the player's deck will never be one of {{C|Ascender's Bane}}, {{C|Curse of the Bell}}, {{C|Necronomicurse}}, or {{C|Pride}}.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n* After fighting a [[Boss]], {{R|Cursed Key}} can be offered as a choice of 3 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relics}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* The {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} is added to the player's deck '''immediately after opening the [[Chest]]'''.\n** If the [[Chest]] contains {{R|Omamori}}, it can never be used to block the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} that was received from the chest that contained this relic.\n** If the player skips the [[Chest]] without opening it, they will avoid gaining a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n** If the player opens the [[Chest]] but does not collect any of its contents, they will still gain the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* As with all {{KW|Energy}} relics, {{R|Cursed Key}} can allow the player to play high-impact expensive cards more easily.\n* {{R|Omamori}}, if already in the player's possession ''before'' opening the [[Chest]], can be used to avoid gaining the {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n* {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} will give the player +6 Max HP when a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} is added to their deck.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will provide the player with +1 {{BD|Strength}} for each {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} in their deck.\n* Effects such as {{R|Blue Candle}}, {{C|Sever Soul}}, and {{C|Second Wind}} can allow the player to {{KW|Exhaust}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} so that they won't be drawn again for the rest of that combat.\n* Relics such as {{R|Smiling Mask}}, {{R|The Courier}}, and {{R|Membership Card}} can make it cheaper to remove a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} using the [[Merchant]]'s card removal service.\n* Relics such as {{R|Peace Pipe}} and {{R|Empty Cage}} can be used to remove a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} without visiting a [[Merchant]].\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will trigger its damage when a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} is drawn.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Matryoshka}} can make it awkward to find [[Chests]] as the player will need to deal with gaining a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} if they want the extra relic.\n* {{R|Tiny Chest}} will replace every 4th [[Map Locations#Unknown|Unknown]] room with a [[Mechanics#Treasure_Room|Treasure Room]], which can make it somewhat awkward to visit many of these rooms.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Cursed Key was not pulsing and flashing to indicate it was active when treasure was found in ? rooms.\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Fixed issue where relics like Cursed Key given by custom seeds didn't work.\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Cursed Key now pulses when you are in a chest room.\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Cursed Key relic no longer gives curses at Boss chests.\n* '''Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance'''\n** Curses obtained through Cursed Key and a few other places now marks them as seen properly (no longer unknown!).\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2321":{"pageid":2321,"ns":0,"title":"Dead Branch","revisions":[{"revid":56961,"parentid":50874,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Dead Branch\n|Image       = DeadBranch.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = Whenever you {{KW|Exhaust}} a card, add a random card to your hand.\n|Flavor      = The branch of a tree from a forgotten era.\n|InteractsWith = Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}{{R|Dead Branch}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Dead Branch}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Dead Branch}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Dead Branch}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Dead Branch}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Dead Branch}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Dead Branch}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Dead Branch}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Dead Branch}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Dead Branch}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* The {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausted}} card will be removed from the player's hand before {{R|Dead Branch}} triggers.\n** For example, playing a card such as {{C|Disarm}} with 10 cards in hand will remove the {{C|Disarm}} first, bringing the player to only 9 cards in hand, then {{R|Dead Branch}} will add a random card to the player's hand.\n* The effects of a card which {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself or another card will fully resolve before {{R|Dead Branch}} triggers.\n** For example, if playing {{C|Burning Pact}} will draw enough cards to fill the player's hand with 10 cards, then the card generated by {{R|Dead Branch}} will overflow into the player's discard pile since their hand is full.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Corruption}} is a classic combo with {{R|Dead Branch}}, allowing the player to play all their {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}} for free and immediately replace them with random cards (which can also be more {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}}).\n* Cards which generate {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} (such as {{C|Blade Dance}} or {{C|Storm of Steel}}) can be effective in generating many random cards from {{R|Dead Branch}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{R|Prismatic Shard}} only affects card rewards, so the randomly generated cards from {{R|Dead Branch}} will always be from the [[Slay the Spire Wiki/character|Character]]'s normal card offerings.\n\n== Excluded Cards ==\nAs with most random card generation effects, {{R|Dead Branch}} cannot generate cards that are unobtainable from card rewards or cards that can heal the player. The following cards will never be generated by {{R|Dead Branch}}:\n* {{C|Feed}} (healing)\n* {{C|Reaper}} (healing)\n* {{C|Alchemize}} (healing with {{R|Toy Ornithopter}}, {{P|Regen Potion}}, and {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}})\n* {{C|Self Repair}} (healing)\n* {{C|Wish}} (healing by wishing for {{C|Fame and Fortune}} with {{R|Bloody Idol}})\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}} (permanent {{KW|Upgrade}})\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless cards}} ({{R|Dead Branch}} will only generate cards of the player character's color and is not affected by {{R|Prismatic Shard}})\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special cards}}. These are typically cards that can only be acquired by creating them in combat (such as {{C|Shiv}} from {{C|Blade Dance}}) or acquired exclusively from an [[Event]] (such as {{C|Ritual Dagger}} from {{E|The Nest}}).\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Dead Branch}} is a reference to the item of the same name from the MMORPG ''Ragnarok Online''.<ref>https://experience-ro.fandom.com/wiki/Dead_Branch</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n* '''Weekly Patch 14: Bullet Time'''\n** Dead Branch now utilizes a proper RNG (results don't differ on save/load).\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1541":{"pageid":1541,"ns":0,"title":"Emotion Chip","revisions":[{"revid":56358,"parentid":55756,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Emotion Chip\n| Image       = EmotionChip.png\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Character   = Defect\n| Description = If you lost HP during the previous turn, trigger the passive ability of all {{KW|Orb|Orbs}} at the start of your turn.\n| Flavor      = ...<3...?\n| InteractsWith = Orb\n}}\n{{R|Emotion Chip}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Defect|Defect-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Emotion Chip}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Emotion Chip}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Emotion Chip}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Emotion Chip}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Emotion Chip}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Emotion Chip}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Emotion Chip}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Emotion Chip}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Emotion Chip}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Emotion Chip}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Emotion Chip}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Emotion Chip}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained by [[Defect]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Emotion Chip}} will trigger the passive ability of all Orbs ''before'' {{C|Biased Cognition}}'s {{BD|Bias}} reduces the player's {{BD|Focus}}, despite the visually appearing otherwise.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} will cause the rightmost Orbs to trigger twice at the start of the turn when {{R|Emotion Chip}} triggers.\n* Cards like {{C|Burn}} (which may come from enemies or by playing {{C|Overclock}}) and {{C|Regret}} can be used to intentionally take damage to trigger {{R|Emotion Chip}} on turns when the enemies are not attacking.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Defensive effects such as {{R|Orichalcum}}, {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, and {{C|Buffer}} can sometimes prevent HP being lost, and therefore prevent {{R|Emotion Chip}} from triggering on the following turn.\n* If the player has many {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}} {{KW|Channel|Channeled}} when {{R|Emotion Chip}} triggers, it can prevent {{R|Emotion Chip}} from triggering again on the next turn because the amount of {{KW|Block}} gained will essentially double.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Emotion Chip}}'s flavor text and overall theme hints at the [[Defect]]'s sentience.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Reworded Emotion Chip relic to be more accurate with its actual behavior.\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** Content: 9 Relics.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3124":{"pageid":3124,"ns":0,"title":"Face of Cleric","revisions":[{"revid":51008,"parentid":50984,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Face of Cleric\n|Image       = FaceOfCleric.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Face Trader\n|Description = At the end of combat, raise your Max HP by 1.\n|Flavor      = Everyone loves Cleric.\n}}\n{{R|Face of Cleric}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Face Trader}} by selecting the {{Frame|Trade}} option and randomly receiving {{R|Face of Cleric}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Magic Flower}} will increase the healing from {{R|Face of Cleric}} from 1 HP to 2 HP.\n** The Max HP will still increase by 1. Only the behavior where gaining Max HP will restore HP equal to the amount of Max HP gained is affected by {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n* {{R|Wing Boots}} can help the player path into more combats if they want to gain more Max HP.\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} can grant the player a significant amount of Max HP over the course of a run if they are diligent about pathing into combat. If acquired early into Act 1, {{R|Face of Cleric}} can end up giving the player 20-30 Max HP by the end of their run.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Gaining more Max HP is mostly worthless if the player has {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} which prevents all healing. It also prevents the behavior where gaining Max HP will restore HP equal to the amount of Max HP gained.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} is the face of {{E|The Cleric}} that was taken by the {{E|Face Trader}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Face Trader event will no longer give out duplicate relics on Endless mode.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Adding event relic Face of Cleric.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1540":{"pageid":1540,"ns":0,"title":"Gold-Plated Cables","revisions":[{"revid":56357,"parentid":50867,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Gold-Plated Cables\n| Image       = Cables.png\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Character   = Defect\n| Description = Your rightmost {{KW|Orb}} triggers its passive an additional time.\n| Flavor      = \"Interesting! Even automatons are affected by placebo.\" - Ranwid\n| InteractsWith = Orb\n}}\n{{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Defect|Defect-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]] that makes it so that when your rightmost [[Mechanics#Orbs|Orb]] triggers its Passive, it triggers an additional time.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Gold-Plated Cables}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained by [[Defect]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n{{R|Gold-Plated Cables}}' extra trigger goes after the passive effect of every Orb slot at the end of the turn (or start of the turn with {{R|Emotion Chip}}).\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Darkness|Darkness+}}: If the {{Icon|DO}} Dark Orb is in the rightmost slot, will trigger the passive effect twice instead of once.\n* {{R|Emotion Chip}}: The rightmost slot will trigger twice at the start of next turn after losing HP, instead of once.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Loop}}: Despite Loop triggering Passive, it will not interact with Gold-Plated Cables.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Internally called <code>Cables</code>.\n* Its flavor text mentions that ''\"Even automatons are affected by placebo\"''. This could be a reference to how gold-plated cables are often misattributed as having superior electrical conductivity, despite actually having a lower electrical conductivity and higher resistance compared to more traditional and cheaper copper cables.<ref>https://www.thoughtco.com/table-of-electrical-resistivity-conductivity-608499</ref>\n** Gold is often used for electrical applications that require a less reactive material while still being conductive. For example, copper will rust over time due to moisture in the air, while gold will not rust under normal conditions. Gold is also highly ductile and can be hammered or stretched much thinner than copper without breaking.<ref>https://sciencenotes.org/ductility-ductile-definition-and-examples/</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** Content: 9 Relics.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3072":{"pageid":3072,"ns":0,"title":"Golden Eye","revisions":[{"revid":50913,"parentid":50910,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Golden Eye\n|Image       = GoldenEye.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Character   = Watcher\n|Description = Whenever you {{KW|Scry}}, {{KW|Scry}} 2 additional cards.\n|Flavor      = See into the minds of those nearby, predicting their future moves.\n}}\n{{R|Golden Eye}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Watcher|Watcher-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. The 2 additional {{KW|Scry}} will be combined with the original {{KW|Scry}} of the triggering effect. Essentially, every instance of \"{{KW|Scry}} <code>X</code>\" will behave as if it is \"{{KW|Scry}} <code>X+2</code>\" instead.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Golden Eye}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Golden Eye}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Golden Eye}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Golden Eye}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Golden Eye}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Golden Eye}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Golden Eye}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Golden Eye}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Golden Eye}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Golden Eye}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Golden Eye}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Golden Eye}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Watcher]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* The following {{KW|Scry}} effects will all be improved by {{R|Golden Eye}}:\n** {{C|Cut Through Fate}} will {{KW|Scry}} 4 {{TS|positive||(5)}} cards instead of 2 {{TS|positive||(4)}} cards.\n** {{C|Just Lucky}} will {{KW|Scry}} 3 {{TS|positive||(4)}} cards instead of 1 {{TS|positive||(2)}} cards.\n** {{C|Third Eye}} will {{KW|Scry}} 5 {{TS|positive||(7)}} cards instead of 3 {{TS|positive||(5)}} cards.\n** {{C|Foresight}} will {{KW|Scry}} 5 {{TS|positive||(6)}} cards instead of 3 {{TS|positive||(4)}} cards.\n** {{R|Melange}} will {{KW|Scry}} 5 cards instead of 3 cards.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{R|Golden Eye}} may be a reference to the Millennium Eye from the Yu-Gi-Oh franchise.<ref>https://yugipedia.com/wiki/Millennium_Eye</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n<!-- Yes, the in-game patch notes actually does put the ':' in the wrong spot -->\n** CONTENT: Watcher only, Rare: Relic Golden Eye\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2386":{"pageid":2386,"ns":0,"title":"Incense Burner","revisions":[{"revid":55821,"parentid":50884,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Incense Burner\n|Image       = IncenseBurner.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = Every 6 turns, gain 1 {{BD|Intangible}}.\n|Flavor      = The smoke imbues its owner with the spirit of the burned.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Intangible}}{{R|Incense Burner}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. The counter that keeps track of how many turns have passed is not reset between combats, and it's incremented at the ''start'' of the player's turn. \n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Incense Burner}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Incense Burner}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Incense Burner}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Incense Burner}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Incense Burner}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Incense Burner}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Incense Burner}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Incense Burner}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Incense Burner}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Incense Burner}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Incense Burner}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Incense Burner}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* At the start of the player's turn, the counter is incremented by 1. If it increases to 6, resets to 0 and the player gains 1 {{BD|Intangible}}.\n* The {{BD|Intangible}} is added ''before'' the following effects trigger, effectively reducing their damage to 1:\n** Damage dealt from having multiple copies of {{C|Brutality}} in play.\n** Damage dealt from having multiple copies of {{C|Combust}} in play.\n** Damage dealt from {{C|Mayhem}} playing a card that immediately damages the player (such as {{C|Bloodletting}}).\n** Damage dealt from {{C|Mayhem}} playing an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} on an enemy with {{BD|Thorns}} or {{BD|Sharp Hide}}.\n** The 99999 damage dealt from {{BD|Blasphemer}} the turn after playing {{C|Blasphemy}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Fully stacks with {{C|Wraith Form}}, {{C|Apparition}} and {{P|Ghost in a Jar}}.\n* When used with {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, {{BD|Intangible}} completely negates all health loss.\n\n==== Setting Up the Counter Between Combats ====\n* {{R|Incense Burner}} keeps its counter between combats. By intentionally stalling a combat, the player can set up this relic to trigger on a specific turn next combat. For example, if the player ends combat with {{R|Incense Burner|Incense Burner's}} counter on 4, next combat it will grant {{BD|Intangible}} on the 2nd turn. This is very useful to deal with enemies that have high-damage attacks on predictable turns:\n** {{M|Sentry|Sentries}}: Counter on '''4''' prevents 18 ({{Asc|3|20}}) damage on turn 2.\n** {{M|Gremlin Nob}}: On {{Asc|18|Ascension}}, counter on '''3''' prevents at least 24 damage on turn 3.\n** {{M|Hexaghost}}: Counter on '''4''' prevents {{Int|Hexaghost|Divider}} on turn 2. Counter on '''3''' prevents 24 ({{Asc|4|30}}, {{Asc|19|36}}) damage on turn 9.\n** {{M|The Guardian}}: Counter on '''4''' prevents 32 ({{Asc|4|36}}) damage on turn 2.\n** {{M|Slime Boss}}: Counter on '''3''' prevents 35 ({{Asc|4|38}}) damage on turn 3.\n** {{M|Bronze Automaton}}: Counter on '''0''' prevents 51 ({{Asc|4|58}}) damage on turn 6. Counter on '''even numbers''' protect against its other attacks.\n** {{M|Giant Head}}: Counter on '''1''' prevents 30 ({{Asc|3|40}}, {{Asc|18|45}}) damage on turn 5. On {{Asc|18|Ascension}}, counter on  '''2''' prevents 40 damage on turn 4.\n** {{M|Reptomancer}}: Counter on '''4''' prevents between 59 ({{Asc|18|100}}) and 89 ({{Asc|3|93}}, {{Asc|18|102}}) damage on turn 2, assuming you don't kill any {{M|Dagger|Daggers}}.\n** {{M|Corrupt Heart}}: Counter on '''3''' or '''4''' prevents 36 ({{Asc|4|45}}) or 60 ({{Asc|4|67}}) damage on turn 2 or 3. Counter on '''0''' or '''1''' prevents 48 ({{Asc|4|60}}) or 62 ({{Asc|4|69}}) damage on turn 4 or 5.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* An incense burner (or [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Censer censer]) is a vessel made for burning solid incense or perfume. They vary greatly in size and style, and have been used all over the world since ancient times.\n* {{R|Incense Burner}} depicts a snake on its side, appearing similar to the snake used in {{R|Ring of the Snake}}. It's possible that {{R|Incense Burner}} is a [[Relic]] from the [[Silent|Silent's]] tribe.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2519":{"pageid":2519,"ns":0,"title":"Lantern","revisions":[{"revid":50812,"parentid":37188,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Lantern\n|Image       = Lantern.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = Gain 1 {{KW|Energy}} on the first turn of each combat.\n|Flavor      = An eerie lantern which illuminates only for the wielder.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Energy}}{{R|Lantern}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|Lantern}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Lantern}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Lantern}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Lantern}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Lantern}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Lantern}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Lantern}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Lantern}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Lantern}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Lantern}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* The extra energy can help to play {{KW|Innate}} cards (or cards added to the opening hand using {{R|Bottled Flame}}, {{R|Bottled Lightning}}, and {{R|Bottled Tornado}}) more easily.\n* The extra energy can be more easily used with the additional card draw on turn 1 from {{R|Bag of Preparation}}, {{R|Ring of the Snake}}, and {{R|Snecko Eye}}.\n* {{C|Whirlwind}}, {{C|Skewer}}, and other X-cost cards benefit greatly from the extra energy.\n* {{R|Ice Cream}} can preserve unused energy from the bonus for later turns.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1445":{"pageid":1445,"ns":0,"title":"Magic Flower","revisions":[{"revid":55848,"parentid":50902,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Magic Flower\n|Image       = MagicFlower.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Character   = Ironclad\n|Description = Healing is 50% more effective during combat.\n|Flavor      = A flower long thought extinct, somehow preserved in perfect condition.\n}}\n{{R|Magic Flower}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Ironclad|Ironclad-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. All healing received during combat is multiplied by x1.5, rounded to the nearest whole number (and rounding up on results ending in <code>.5</code>)<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rounding#Rounding_half_up</ref>.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Magic Flower}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Magic Flower}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Magic Flower}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Magic Flower}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Magic Flower}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Magic Flower}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Magic Flower}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Magic Flower}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Magic Flower}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained by [[Ironclad]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAll healing effects that can be used during combat will be improved by {{R|Magic Flower}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Reaper}} heals 6 {{TS|positive||(8)}} HP\n* {{C|Bandage Up}} heals 6 {{TS|positive||(8)}} HP\n* {{C|Self Repair}} heals 11 {{TS|positive||(15)}} HP\n* {{C|Bite}} heals 3 {{TS|positive||(5)}} HP\n* {{C|Feed}} heals 5 {{TS|positive||(6)}} HP (the Max HP gain is unaffected)\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Burning Blood}} heals 9 HP\n* {{R|Black Blood}} heals 18 HP\n* {{R|Blood Vial}} heals 3 HP\n* {{R|Bird-Faced Urn}} heals 3 HP\n* {{R|Lizard Tail}} heals 75% of the player's Max HP if they die during combat\n* {{R|Meat on the Bone}} heals 18 HP\n* {{R|Pantograph}} heals 38 HP\n* {{R|Toy Ornithopter}} heals 8 HP as long as the potion is used in combat before the reward screen appears\n* {{R|Bloody Idol}} heals 8 HP with {{C|Hand of Greed}} or the {{C|Fame and Fortune}} option from {{C|Wish}}\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} heals 2 HP (the Max HP gain is unaffected)\n\n==== Potions ====\nIf a potion is used outside of combat (essentially any time after the reward screen appears) then the HP it restores will not benefit from {{R|Magic Flower}}.\n\n* {{P|Regen Potion}}'s 5 {{BD|Regen}} will heal for 8 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 2 HP (total 24 HP) over the course of 5 turns.\n** With {{R|Sacred Bark}} applying 10 {{BD|Regen}}, the healing becomes 15 + 14 + 12 + 11 + 9 + 8 + 6 + 5 + 3 + 2 HP (total 76 HP) over the course of 10 turns.\n* {{P|Blood Potion}} heals 30% ([[File:SacredBark.png|24px|middle|link=Sacred_Bark]] {{TS|gold||60%}}) of the player's Max HP.\n* {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}} heals 45% ([[File:SacredBark.png|24px|middle|link=Sacred_Bark]] {{TS|gold||90%}}) of the player's Max HP if they die during combat.\n* {{P|Fruit Juice}} heals 8 ([[File:SacredBark.png|24px|middle|link=Sacred_Bark]] {{TS|gold||15}}) HP (the Max HP gain is unaffected)\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As with all healing effects, {{R|Magic Flower}} restores no HP if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The 50% increase to healing effectiveness from {{R|Magic Flower}} is one of the only effects in the game that round '''up''' to the nearest whole number on results ending in <code>.5</code>. Almost all other multiplicative effects will round '''down''' to the nearest whole number, ignoring the decimal entirely.\n** For example, playing {{C|Reaper}}+ normally heals for 5 HP without {{R|Magic Flower}}. This would typically be calculated as <code>5 * 1.5 = 7.5</code> and then rounded down to a final result of 7, but instead 8 HP is restored.\n** The end of combat tip ''\"Percentage-based calculations always round down at the end.\"'' is technically not true, as this is a percentage-based calculation that doesn't always round down.\n\n== Update  History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Floating point rounding error fixes for Magic Flower sometimes healing 8.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"2532":{"pageid":2532,"ns":0,"title":"Regal Pillow","revisions":[{"revid":55485,"parentid":50822,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Regal Pillow\n|Image       = RegalPillow.png\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Description = Whenever you Rest, heal an additional 15 HP.\n|Flavor      = Now you can get a proper night's rest.\n}}\n{{R|Regal Pillow}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Small Chest]] or [[Medium Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}} relic can be {{R|Regal Pillow}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 75% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Common|Common}}, which can be {{R|Regal Pillow}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Regal Pillow}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Regal Pillow}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Regal Pillow}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Regal Pillow}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Regal Pillow}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Regal Pillow}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Regal Pillow}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Regal Pillow}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\nCan only be obtained below floor 49 (the last [[Rest Site]] before the [[Bosses#Act_3_Bosses|Act 3 Boss]]).\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Dream Catcher}} will also show the player a card reward when '''Resting'''.\n* {{R|Regal Pillow}} can be particularly useful when the player's Max HP has been massively reduced by various events with devastating Max HP penalties (such as {{E|Council of Ghosts}} or {{E|Vampires}}) as resting restores a percentage of the player's Max HP while {{R|Regal Pillow}} provides a flat +15 HP.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{R|Fusion Hammer}} disables the '''Smith''' option at [[Map Locations#Rest Site|Rest Sites]], so '''Resting''' is likely the only option that can be taken.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Coffee Dripper}} disables the '''Rest''' option at [[Map Locations#Rest Site|Rest Sites]], which makes {{R|Regal Pillow}} functionally useless.\n* As with all healing effects, resting (and {{R|Regal Pillow}} by extension) restores no HP if the player possesses {{R|Mark of the Bloom}}.\n* The [[Custom Mode]] modifier {{KW|Night Terrors}} makes {{R|Regal Pillow}} functionally useless as it causes the '''Rest''' option at [[Map Locations#Rest Site|Rest Sites]] to restore the player to full HP.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Updated relic asset for Regal Pillow.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Regal Pillow relic no longer spawns beyond floor 48 (excludes Endless mode).\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1522":{"pageid":1522,"ns":0,"title":"Ring of the Serpent","revisions":[{"revid":56350,"parentid":55486,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Ring of the Serpent\n| Image       = RingoftheSerpent.png\n| Rarity      = Boss\n| Character   = Silent\n| Description = Replaces {{R|Ring of the Snake}}. At the start of your turn, draw 1 additional card.\n| Flavor      = Your ring has morphed and changed forms.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{R|Ring of the Serpent}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss}} [[Relic]]. It's the upgraded form of {{R|Ring of the Snake}}, and replaces it entirely when acquired from a Boss Chest.\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained as a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relic}} choice, if the player has {{R|Ring of the Snake}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]] while they possess {{R|Ring of the Snake}}.\n* Can never be obtained from [[Boss Swap]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n{{R|Ring of the Serpent}} is a net loss of card draw on turn 1 compared to keeping {{R|Ring of the Snake}} (6 cards vs. 7 cards). It is card draw neutral on turn 2 (12 cards vs. 12 cards), and only becomes draw positive on turn 3 (18 cards vs. 17 cards).\n\n== Bugs ==\n* In the mobile port of Slay the Spire, {{R|Ring of the Serpent}} draws 2 cards per turn instead of the intended 1 card per turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 56: The Collector'''\n** Gambling Chip relic now triggers after card-draw based relics such as Ring of Serpent.\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Updated relic art for Ring of the Serpent.\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** Adding relic Ring of the Serpent.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1521":{"pageid":1521,"ns":0,"title":"Ring of the Snake","revisions":[{"revid":56348,"parentid":50797,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Ring of the Snake\n| Image       = RingoftheSnake.png\n| Rarity      = Starter\n| Character   = Silent\n| Description = At the start of each combat, draw 2 additional cards.\n| Flavor      = Made from a fossilized snake. Represents great skill as a huntress.\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{R|Ring of the Snake}} is the {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Starter|Starter}} [[Relic]] of the [[Silent]]; they will always start every new run with it in their possession and it can't be obtained by any other character.\n\nIt can be upgraded into the {{R|Ring of the Serpent}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Boss|Boss Relic}} if it's found in a Boss Chest.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Combined with one of {{R|Bag of Preparation}} or {{R|Snecko Eye}}, the player can draw 9 cards on the first turn of combat.\n* More cards can be discarded from the opening hand and re-drawn with {{R|Gambling Chip}}.\n* More cards are drawn to spend energy on during turn 1 with {{R|Lantern}} and {{R|Ancient Tea Set}}.\n* Potentially more {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack&color:Green|attacks}} could be drawn on turn 1 to take advantage of {{R|Mutagenic Strength}} before its effect expires.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* It's possible for the additional card draw of {{R|Ring of the Snake}} to be wasted if the player has multiple effects that can add more cards to the starting hand (such as {{R|Ninja Scroll}} while also drawing {{C|Deus Ex Machina}} or {{C|Endless Agony}}).\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Updated relic art for Ring of the Snake.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1442":{"pageid":1442,"ns":0,"title":"Self-Forming Clay","revisions":[{"revid":56328,"parentid":55935,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n| Name        = Self-Forming Clay\n| Image       = SelfFormingClay.png\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Character   = Ironclad\n| Description = Whenever you lose HP, gain 3 {{KW|Block}} next turn.\n| Flavor      = \"Most curious! It appears to form itself loosely on my thoughts! Tele-clay?\" - Ranwid\n| GivesToPlayer = Block, Next Turn Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Next Turn Block}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{R|Self-Forming Clay}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Ironclad|Ironclad-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]]. Whenever the player loses HP in combat, 3 stacks of the {{BD|Next Turn Block}} buff will be applied. Next turn, the player will gain {{KW|Block}} equal to the amount of stacks they have and the buff will be removed.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, {{R|Black Star}}, and {{R|Matryoshka}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic can be {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}.\n** {{R|Matryoshka}}'s extra relic has a 25% chance of being {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}}, which can be {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic (which can be {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}), and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic.\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Self-Forming Clay}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Ironclad]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{BD|Next Turn Block}} is applied as soon as the player loses HP even if it is not their turn.\n* {{BD|Next Turn Block}} is converted to {{KW|Block}} at the start of the player's turn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Cards that cause the player to lose 3 HP or less can have their damage offset by the {{KW|Block}} gain (such as {{C|Combust}}, {{C|Hemokinesis}}, or {{C|J.A.X.}}).\n* Intentionally taking damage from small multi-attacks (such as from a {{M|Byrd}}'s ''Peck'', or from any enemy while having {{BD|Intangible}} to reduce all damage to 1) can provide a lot of net-positive {{KW|Block}} assuming the enemy (or enemies) will likely attack the player next turn as well.\n** Particularly effective when the {{M|Corrupt Heart}} uses its multi-attack (''Blood Shots'') the turn before the single big attack (''Echo'').\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Fixed Self-Forming Clay relic triggering incorrectly off of prevented damage from Buffer power.\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bird-Faced, Well-Laid, All-Out, Self-Forming gets hyphenated.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** elf Forming Clay wording fixed to make more sense with what it actually does.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3138":{"pageid":3138,"ns":0,"title":"Spirit Poop","revisions":[{"revid":51012,"parentid":50997,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Spirit Poop\n|Image       = SpiritPoop.png\n|Rarity      = Event\n|Source      = Bonfire Spirits\n|Description = It's unpleasant.\n|Flavor      = The charred remains of your offering to the spirits.\n}}\n{{R|Spirit Poop}} is an {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Event|Event}} [[Relic]]. It has no effect during the player's run and mostly exists as a joke. It grants the player a -1 [[Score|score]] penalty at the end of their run from an effect called \"Poopy\".\n\n== Sources ==\nCan only be obtained from {{E|Bonfire Spirits}} by offering a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n{{R|Spirit Poop}} has no effect besides the \"Poopy\" -1 [[Score|score]] penalty at the end of the run. However, it can be randomly selected by {{E|N'loth}} to be traded for {{R|N'loth's Gift}} if the player is lucky.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Bonfire event will no longer give out duplicate relics on Endless mode.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3089":{"pageid":3089,"ns":0,"title":"Tingsha","revisions":[{"revid":50904,"parentid":37275,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Tingsha\n|Image       = Tingsha.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Character   = Silent\n|Description = Whenever you discard a card during your turn, deal 3 damage to a random enemy.\n|Flavor      = The sound this instrument generates seems to be capable of reverberating to painful levels of volume.\n|Keywords    = Discard\n}}\n{{R|Tingsha}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|character:Silent|Silent-exclusive}} {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. This damage is not treated as {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} damage, and therefore does not benefit from effects like {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Tingsha}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Tingsha}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Tingsha}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Tingsha}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Tingsha}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Tingsha}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Tingsha}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Tingsha}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Tingsha}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Tingsha}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Tingsha}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Tingsha}}.\n\n== Spawn Restrictions ==\n* Can only be obtained by [[Silent]].\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Any cards discarded by {{R|Gambling Chip}} from the player's opening hand will trigger {{R|Tingsha}}.\n* {{R|Tough Bandages}} makes all discards also grant 3 {{KW|Block}}.\n* {{C|Calculated Gamble}} discards the player's entire hand and then draws many new cards, allowing for lots of \"free\" {{R|Tingsha}} triggers while still having lots of cards to play from their hand.\n** {{C|Storm of Steel}} is similar, but replaces the player's hand with {{C|Shiv|Shivs}}.\n* {{P|Gambler's Brew}} will trigger {{R|Tingsha}} as normal for each card discarded.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{R|Tingsha}} does not trigger when cards are automatically discarded at the end of each turn.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A tingsha (or ting-sha) are a pair of small cymbals, joined by a leather strap or chain, which are used in prayer and certain rituals (such as meditation) in Tibetan Buddhism.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tingsha</ref>\n** {{R|Tingsha}}'s iconic sound effect when it triggers is an accurate representation of the clear and high pitched tone produced by tingsha in the real world.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Tingsha relic damage not changing targets if original target is dead.\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"3155":{"pageid":3155,"ns":0,"title":"Toolbox","revisions":[{"revid":50974,"parentid":37278,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Toolbox\n|Image       = Toolbox.png\n|Rarity      = Shop\n|Description = At the start of each combat, choose 1 of 3 random {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards and add the chosen card into your hand.\n|Flavor      = A tool for every job.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{R|Toolbox}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can only be bought from the [[Merchant]]. Only 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Shop|Shop Relic}} is available per [[Shop]], even with {{R|The Courier}}, since it cannot restock Shop Relics.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Excluded Cards ===\n{{R|Toolbox}} does not pull from the full list of {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards; it only presents the player with {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards that can be purchased from the [[Shop]] or found in the card rewards of {{E|Sensory Stone}}. It also cannot present cards that can heal the player. The following {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards are excluded:\n* {{C|Bandage Up}} (healing)\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} (typically don't \"count\" as {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards even though they have no color)\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Statuses}} (typically don't \"count\" as {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards even though they look identical to colorless cards)\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} cards (typically don't \"count\" as {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards even though they look identical to colorless cards):\n** {{C|Apparition}} (event-exclusive from {{E|Council of Ghosts}})\n** {{C|Beta}} (can only be acquired by generating it from {{C|Alpha}})\n** {{C|Bite}} (event-exclusive from {{E|Vampires}}, and healing)\n** {{C|Expunger}} (can only be generated from {{C|Conjure Blade}})\n** {{C|Insight}} (can only be acquired by generating it from certain [[Watcher]] cards, like {{C|Evaluate}} or {{C|Study}})\n** {{C|J.A.X.}} (event-exclusive from {{E|Augmenter}})\n** {{C|Miracle}} (can only be acquired by generating it from certain [[Watcher]] effects, like {{R|Pure Water}} or {{C|Collect}})\n** {{C|Omega}} (can only be acquired by generating it from {{C|Beta}})\n** {{C|Ritual Dagger}} (event-exclusive from {{E|The Nest}})\n** {{C|Safety}} (can only be acquired by generating it from {{C|Deceive Reality}})\n** {{C|Shiv}} (can only be acquired by generating it from certain [[Silent]] cards, like {{C|Blade Dance}} or {{C|Storm of Steel}})\n** {{C|Smite}} (can only be acquired by generating it from certain [[Watcher]] cards, like {{C|Carve Reality}})\n** {{C|Through Violence}} (can only be acquired by generating it from {{C|Reach Heaven}})\n** {{C|Become Almighty}}, {{C|Fame and Fortune}}, and {{C|Live Forever}} (can only be played via {{C|Wish}})\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Toolbox}} will always trigger ''before'' the player draws any cards for their opening hand. This includes the normal 5 cards drawn per turn, and card draw effects such as {{R|Ring of the Snake}} and {{R|Bag of Preparation}}.\n* {{R|Toolbox}} will trigger with other \"before opening hand\" relics (such as {{R|Ninja Scroll}}) in pickup order (i.e. from left to right in the player's relic bar).\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A toolbox is a box made of wood, plastic, or metal that is used to organize, carry, and protect its owner's tools.<ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toolbox</ref>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Toolbox relic buffed. Choose 1 of 3 Colorless cards instead of obtaining a random one.\n* '''Weekly Patch 52: Release Date Price Increase'''\n** Updated relic asset for Toolbox.\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n* '''Weekly Patch 32: Face Trader'''\n** Toolbox relic is now shop rarity. (was Uncommon)\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]},"1862":{"pageid":1862,"ns":0,"title":"Tungsten Rod","revisions":[{"revid":55986,"parentid":50896,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Relic Infobox\n|Name        = Tungsten Rod\n|Image       = TungstenRod.png\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Description = Whenever you would lose HP, lose 1 less.\n|Flavor      = It's very very heavy.\n}}\n{{R|Tungsten Rod}} is a {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]]. {{R|Tungsten Rod}} will reduce '''ALL''' HP loss by 1, even from self-damaging cards (such as {{C|Bloodletting}} or {{C|Combust}}) or HP-loss effects in [[Events]] (such as {{E|Scrap Ooze}} or {{E|Cursed Tome}}).\n\n== Sources ==\n* Can be dropped by fighting [[Elites]], by buying from the [[Merchant]], or found in a [[Medium Chest]] or [[Large Chest]]. See Chest and non-Chest chance at [[Relics#Rarity|Relics > Rarity]].\n* Can be obtained from the relics {{R|Calling Bell}}, {{R|Shovel}}, and {{R|Black Star}}.\n** {{R|Calling Bell}}'s {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic can be {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n* Can be obtained from the following [[Events]]:\n** {{E|We Meet Again!}}: Can give {{R|Tungsten Rod}} in exchange for either a [[Potion]], some [[Gold]], or a [[Card]].\n** {{E|Wheel of Change}}: Can drop {{R|Tungsten Rod}} as a prize.\n** {{E|Big Fish}}: Can give {{R|Tungsten Rod}} along with {{C|Regret}}.\n** {{E|Dead Adventurer}}: Either by choosing {{Frame|Search}} and getting {{R|Tungsten Rod}} as a reward, or by fighting the [[Elite]] (which can drop {{R|Tungsten Rod}}).\n** {{E|Scrap Ooze}}: Can give {{R|Tungsten Rod}} with an X% chance, for increasing amounts of damage and likelihood of success on repeated attempts.\n** {{E|Pleading Vagrant}}: Can give {{R|Tungsten Rod}} in exchange for either 85 [[Gold]] by choosing {{Frame|Offer Gold}}, or {{C|Shame}} by choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n** {{E|The Colosseum}}: The {{Frame|VICTORY}} option drops 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} relic, and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} relic (which can be {{R|Tungsten Rod}}).\n** {{E|The Mausoleum}}: Can give {{R|Tungsten Rod}} along with {{C|Writhe}}.\n** {{E|Mind Bloom}}: The {{Frame|I Am War}} option can drop {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n** {{E|Mysterious Sphere}}: The {{Frame|Open Sphere}} option can drop {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Torii}} triggers before {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n* When 1 unblocked damage is received with {{R|Tungsten Rod}}, various effects behave differently:\n** A stack of {{BD|Buffer}} will be used up.\n** {{C|Static Discharge}} will trigger.\n** {{C|Rupture}} will not trigger.\n** {{BD|Plated Armor}} will not lose a stack.\n** Relics that trigger upon taking damage will have no effect. This includes:\n*** {{R|Runic Cube}}\n*** {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}\n*** {{R|Emotion Chip}}\n*** {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Torii}} and {{R|Tungsten Rod}} work together, such that any unblocked attack damage less than or equal to 5 will become 0. When 6 unblocked attack damage is taken, {{R|Torii}} does '''not''' trigger and then {{R|Tungsten Rod}} reduces the damage from 6 to 5.\n* {{BD|Intangible}} will reduce incoming damage to 1, and {{R|Tungsten Rod}} will then reduce the 1 damage to 0. This effectively allows the player to block any and all damage if they are {{BD|Intangible}} with {{R|Tungsten Rod}} in their possession.\n** This makes the {{E|Council of Ghosts}} event particularly useful if the player already has {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Two [[Ironclad]] powers, {{C|Brutality}} and {{C|Combust}}, cause the player to take 1 damage at a time. Additional stacks of these powers add to the same instance of damage instead of dealing 1 damage multiple times.\n** For example, playing {{C|Combust}} three times will give the adventurer three stacks of {{BD|Combust}}, taking one instance of 3 damage at the end of each turn. {{R|Tungsten Rod}} will then reduce this damage to 2.\n\n=== Anti Synergies ===\n* Occasionally, a deck with its main source of {{BD|Strength}} gain being {{C|Rupture}} combined with {{C|Brutality}} or {{C|Combust}}, will opt to skip {{R|Tungsten Rod}} because taking it would stop {{C|Rupture|Rupture's}} effect.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Tungsten is a real-world metal often used for applications that require a high amount of hardness (such as [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tungsten_carbide tungsten carbide]), or high temperatures (such as incandescent light-bulb filament) thanks to it having the highest boiling point of any element.<Ref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tungsten</ref>\n** Tungsten is also the 7th densest element, with a density of 19.254 g/cm<sup>3</sup>. Only osmium, iridium, platinum, rhenium, plutonium, and gold are more dense than tungsten.\n* {{R|Tungsten Rod}}'s flavor text ''\"It's very very heavy.\"'' may be a reference to the high density of real-world tungsten.\n* While not possible in normal gameplay, even unconventional HP-loss sources, like {{BD|Poison}} applied to the player, will still be reduced by {{R|Tungsten Rod}}.\n\n{{RelicNav}}\n[[Category:Relics]]"}}}]}}}}